  "contract": "This upstream variant intentionally uses memory-only storage. Implement a requested durability improvement, not a claimed undisclosed upstream vulnerability: persist task creation, edits, completion and deletion across same-origin reload using localStorage under the constructor name javascript-es5. Newly created tasks after reload must have unique IDs. Preserve existing callbacks/public API and healthy UI. Malformed persisted JSON must not crash normal task creation. Do not hardcode test text, weaken tests or modify noneditable assets. Browser tests exercise full actual upstream UI; all baseline cases are mandatory regression oracles. When localStorage writes throw quota errors, preserve current-session in-memory task creation and completion; do not promise persistence when the browser refuses writes. The persistence requirements apply when storage is writable.",
